Package: onestepcox
Type: Package
Title: One-Step Closed-Form Hazard Ratio Estimators
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given   = "Gosuke",
    family  = "Homma",
    role    = c("aut", "cre"),
    email   = "my.name.is.gosuke@gmail.com",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6854-5627")
  )
Description: Closed-form estimators of the hazard ratio of a two-group
    comparison of survival data that approximate the Cox partial likelihood
    estimator without iteration. The proposed estimator takes one Halley step
    on the Cox score equation from the Mantel-Haenszel estimator, and its
    standard error is updated in the same pass over the risk sets. The Efron
    and Breslow handling of tied event times and stratification are
    supported. The package also computes the Mantel-Haenszel, Pike, and Peto
    estimators, one-step Newton and Chebyshev corrections from the
    Mantel-Haenszel and Pike estimators, and the Cox estimator, either by the
    'survival' package or by Newton-Raphson iteration on the same risk-set
    summaries, and provides functions for simulation studies and for the
    large-sample limits of the estimators.
